":"p","attribute":"","kind":"text","legacy_name":"copy_blog_single_005"},{"name":"copy_blog_single_0028","label":"P 0028 — Successful systems start by codifying foundational primitives — color va","default":"Successful systems start by codifying foundational primitives — color variables, typographic scales, spacing rhythms, and responsive grid rules — before building complex organisms.","tag":"p","attribute":"","kind":"text","legacy_name":"copy_blog_single_006"},{"name":"copy_blog_single_0029","label":"P 0029 — When product managers, designers, and engineers share the exact same voc","default":"When product managers, designers, and engineers share the exact same vocabulary for spacing, elevation, and interactive states, handoff friction disappears and visual consistency becomes automatic.","tag":"p","attribute":"","kind":"text","legacy_name":"copy_blog_single_007"},{"name":"copy_blog_single_0030","label":"H2 0030 — 2. Structuring a Token-First CSS Architecture","default":"2. Structuring a Token-First CSS Architecture","tag":"h2","attribute":"","kind":"text","legacy_name":"copy_blog_single_008"},{"name":"copy_blog_single_0031","label":"P 0031 — By anchoring every component to semantic custom properties, engineering ","default":"By anchoring every component to semantic custom properties, engineering teams gain effortless maintainability. Updating a primary brand hue or typographic hierarchy cascades cleanly across headers, cards, drawers, and interactive states.","tag":"p","attribute":"","kind":"text","legacy_name":"copy_blog_single_009"},{"name":"copy_blog_single_0032","label":"SPAN 0032 — Define strict root color and font primitives before component styling.","default":"Define strict root color and font primitives before component styling.","tag":"span","attribute":"","kind":"text"},{"name":"copy_blog_single_0033","label":"SPAN 0033 — Separate global layout chrome from reusable UI components.","default":"Separate global layout chrome from reusable UI components.","t